    {
      "id": "claim_8db8a321da1d495ca383300eaa15c8a9",
      "statement": "Per active-program slot, recommendationForSlot() applies a fixed guardrail order: significant joint pain in the current window suppresses all slots and returns a single pain_review recommendation first; then an effective deload phase (via resolvePrescription()+isDeload()) returns deload_hold; then two consecutive harder-than-target first sets return an effort-based reduce_load; then a stall-report plateau whose latest stalled point matches the latest exposure returns plateau_review; then one down exposure (>1% below only the immediately preceding exposure) returns keep_movement instead of a plateau/swap call; only then does normal sessionTarget() double progression apply; a slot with no finished linked exposure returns insufficient_data instead of a cross-exercise estimate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/COACH-REPORT.md#L105-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:959baa1667f769895d70b5fb2a7a7ee656332cf4694d055808207cd2eac514a6:"
